<section class="retreat-hero">
  <p class="retreat-hero__eyebrow">October 16–18, 2026 · Woodlands Retreat · Nunnelly, Tennessee</p>
  <h1>The First Christian Transhumanist Retreat</h1>
  <p class="retreat-hero__sub">Three days on 300 wooded acres — a lake, trails, a chapel, fire and conversation late into the night. Fewer talks, more table.</p>
  <div class="retreat-hero__cta">
    <a class="retreat-btn" href="#register">Register</a>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-intro">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <p>For ten years we've gathered online and on conference stages to ask one question together: what does it mean to follow Christ into the future? This fall, for the first time, we're taking that question into the woods. A retreat, not a conference — less presenting, more presence.</p>
    <p>We'll come to embody the thing we keep pointing at — a hopeful, rational, future-facing faith — before we argue another word about it.</p>
    <p>We work against illness, hunger, oppression, injustice, and death — and once a year, it's good to do that work shoulder to shoulder, in person, with people who see what you see.</p>
    <p class="retreat-theme-line">The theme that will hold our weekend: <strong>the shape of progress is the face of Christ.</strong> Come find out what we mean.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="retreat-section retreat-details">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>The details</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>When:</strong> Friday, October 16 (check-in 4pm) → Sunday, October 18 (10am)</li>
      <li><strong>Where:</strong> Woodlands Retreat, Nunnelly, TN — about an hour west of Nashville. Lodge bedding provided.</li>
      <li><strong>Who:</strong> the CTA community and friends — space is limited</li>
      <li><strong>Meals:</strong> dinner Friday and Saturday; shared breakfasts and lunch</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>

<a id="register"></a>
<section class="retreat-section retreat-section--wide retreat-register">
  <div class="retreat-section__inner">
    <h2>Register</h2>
    <p class="retreat-register__lede">Every registration includes the full weekend — lodging, meals, and everything we do together. The only difference between tiers is the room you sleep in. The crossed-out price is the true price of the weekend; generous donors and volunteers have worked hard to make it this accessible.</p>
    <div class="retreat-tiers">
      {% for tier in tiers %}
      <div class="tier-card">
        {% if tier.badge %}<span class="tier-card__badge">{{ tier.badge }}</span>{% endif %}
        <h3>{{ tier.name }}</h3>
        <p class="tier-card__detail">{{ tier.detail }}</p>
        <ul class="tier-options">
          {% for opt in tier.options %}
          <li class="tier-option{% if opt.unavailable %} tier-option--unavailable{% endif %}">
            <span class="tier-option__text">
              <span class="tier-option__label">{{ opt.label }}{% if opt.note %} <span class="tier-option__note">· {{ opt.note }}</span>{% endif %}</span>
              <span class="tier-option__price"><s>{{ opt.wasPrice }}</s> {{ opt.price }}</span>
            </span>
            {% if opt.unavailable %}
            <span class="tier-option__flag">Unavailable</span>
            {% else %}
            <a class="retreat-btn" href="{{ opt.url }}">Register</a>
            {% endif %}
          </li>
          {% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    <p class="retreat-register__scholarship">We don't want money to be the reason anyone stays home. <strong>Scholarships are available — just ask.</strong> And if you'd like to help make that possible for someone else, by giving or by volunteering at the retreat, tell us that too. Either way, write us: <a href="mailto:admin@christiantranshumanism.org?subject=CTA%20Retreat">admin@christiantranshumanism.org</a></p>
  </div>
</section>

